To update the Top Right Quadrant (Benefits / MOE / ROI) to satisfy your manager, you need to pivot the language from Technical Metrics (latency, query speed, ontology time) to Business Outcomes (Cost, Risk, Yield).
Here is a proposed rewrite of that section. You can copy and paste this structure into your slide.
Revised Section: Benefits / Measure of Effectiveness (MOE) / ROI
1. Business Problem: Slow Root Cause Analysis (Failure ID)
	Metric (MOE): Mean Time to Identify (MTTI) defects.
	Improvement: Reduced data retrieval from 2 days (48hrs) 
<5 seconds.
	Business KPI Impact: Accelerated Failure Identification reduces WIP held in quarantine; enables faster corrective action to stop scrap/rework generation.
2. Business Problem: Cost of Poor Quality (COPQ)
	Metric (MOE): Cross-system Defect Correlation (Multi-hop complexity).
	Improvement: Enables correlation of Order Volume (SAP) vs Test Rates (MES) vs Defects (QMS).
	Business KPI Impact: Improved First Pass Yield (FPY) by identifying complex failure modes invisible to single-system queries.
3. Business Problem: High Engineering Overhead
	Metric (MOE): Data Integration Cycle Time.
	Improvement: Automated mapping reduces integration time from 6-18 months 
1 month.
	Business KPI Impact: OpEx Savings: Avoidance of 
	        80k-
      
280k in manual data engineering costs per data source; reallocation of talent to process improvement.
4. Business Problem: Regulatory & Compliance Risk
	Metric (MOE): Audit Trail Determinism.
	Improvement: Move from probabilistic (vector) search 
	        →
      
Deterministic Knowledge Graph.
	Business KPI Impact: Ensures AS9100/FDA auditability; establishes a "Single Source of Truth" for compliance reporting.
________________________________________
How this changes your "ROI per Site" section:
	Current: KG dev acceleration: $x/yr
	Update: Engineering Cost Avoidance: $80k - $280k per integration.
	Current: Faster decisions: $z/yr
	Update: Scrap/Rework Reduction: [Insert % or $ Estimate] via faster root cause ID.
	Current: Analyst productivity: $xyr
	Update: Analyst Throughput: 10x increase in queries answered per day.
________________________________________
Why this works for your Manager:
	It names the problem first: It doesn't just say "we are faster"; it says "we are fixing the slow root cause analysis problem."
	It uses standard KPIs: Managers care about MTTI (Mean Time to Identify), WIP (Work in Progress), FPY (First Pass Yield), and OpEx (Operating Expense).
	It explicitly links speed to money: It connects the 5-second query time directly to reduced quarantine inventory.


